================================================================================
Context → Pages: render page preview body as HTML, not Markdown
================================================================================

Context:
The preview modal showed the Knowledge Page body as escaped plain text. The
body is HTML and must render as HTML, not be parsed as Markdown. Rendering uses
DOMPurify (already loaded in base.html) so untrusted markup cannot run scripts
or event handlers; without DOMPurify it falls back to escaped plain text.

Changes:

1. src/front/static/domain/js/domain-pages.js
   Preview body rendered via new `_renderPageHtml` (DOMPurify.sanitize, HTML
   profile). Empty bodies show "(empty body)"; no marked/renderMarkdown.
2. src/front/static/domain/css/domain-pages.css
   Dropped pre-wrap from the preview container; added image/table rules and a
   pre-wrap class only for the plain-text fallback.
3. tests/units/front/test_domain_pages_contract.py
   Contract: preview uses sanitized HTML, not Markdown or escaped body.

