================================================================================
Fix: pattern detection job fails on Spark ANSI cast (CAST_INVALID_INPUT)
================================================================================

Context
-------
The Databricks job `ontobricks-10x-pattern-detection` failed in task
`detect_patterns` with
`[CAST_INVALID_INPUT] The value 'AGT138' of the type "STRING" cannot be cast to "DOUBLE"`.
Serverless compute runs Spark in ANSI mode, where casting non-numeric text
raises, whereas the SQLite test harness casts leniently and hid the bug.
Two causes in `PatternSQL.build_bins`: (1) the ranking window did
`ORDER BY CAST(value AS DOUBLE)` over every property, not just numeric ones;
(2) the "is numeric" gate was too loose (dates like 2026-11-13 and versions
like 1.2.3 slipped through).

Changes
-------
1. src/jobs/graph_analytics_job.py - `_portable_is_numeric_sql` is now strict:
   only plain decimals (optional leading '-', at most one '.').
2. src/jobs/graph_analytics_job.py - `build_bins` ranking subquery joins
   `prop_kind` and only reads properties classified `num`, so the DOUBLE cast
   never sees categorical values.
3. tests/units/core/test_pattern_job_sql.py - harness variant that raises on
   invalid DOUBLE casts (mimics ANSI); `TestStrictCastSafety` (ids, dates,
   versions stay categorical; real numerics still binned) and
   `TestPortableIsNumeric` (edge cases of the gate).

Modified files
--------------
- src/jobs/graph_analytics_job.py
- tests/units/core/test_pattern_job_sql.py

Tests
-----
uv run --frozen pytest -q -m "not scenario" -> 10472 passed, 323 skipped, 8 deselected.
Requires `make deploy` / `make deploy-no-run` so the job picks up the new script.

================================================================================
Fix: pattern detection returned "0 patterns" - automatic signature detail levels
================================================================================

Context
-------
After the ANSI cast fix the Databricks job ran to completion but reported
"0 patterns over 200 anchors" (Cust360Auto Customer, 3 hops, min support 3).
Reproduced against the real triple table with the work tables kept: the exact
token multiset was unique for every customer. Causes: (1) identifier-like
attributes (customerid, email, phone, street, first name, dates) gave the top
20 values their own label, so those anchors were unique even at hop 0;
(2) exact neighbour counts plus neighbour attribute bins over 3 hops made each
signature unique (hop 0 alone: 193 distinct signatures out of 200). Measured
on the real data: structure-only signatures give 16 patterns covering 136 of
200 customers, attribute-including signatures give <= 3 patterns.
After the fix the same run yields 17 patterns covering 140 of 200 customers.

Changes
-------
1. src/jobs/graph_analytics_job.py - categorical attributes with more than 20
   distinct values (CATEGORICAL_MAX_VALUES) are ignored instead of being binned
   into top-20 + "__other".
2. src/jobs/graph_analytics_job.py - tokens table gains a `hop` column;
   `PatternSQL.level_filter` / `build_signatures(level)` hash the tokens kept at
   a detail level (full = exact multiset; neighbour / own / structure = token
   set). Anchors with no token at a level hash the empty set (isolated pattern).
3. src/jobs/graph_analytics_job.py - `_choose_detail_level` walks
   PATTERN_LEVELS finest-first and keeps the first level whose patterns cover
   >= 50% of the anchors (structure is the floor). `_run_pattern_stages` split
   into `_expand_neighbourhoods` + `_choose_detail_level`; refine only runs at
   the full level; shapes list only the tokens of the chosen level; summary
   table gains `detail_level`.
4. src/back/core/graph_analysis/JobPatterns.py - summary read-back exposes
   `detail_level`.
5. src/front/static/simulation/js/simulation-patterns.js - "Detail" stat
   (Exact / Neighbours (1 hop) / Own attributes / Structure only).
6. tests - TestDetailLevels (identifier-like attribute ignored, fallback to
   structure, stays exact when exact works, multiplicity ignored at coarse
   levels, isolated anchors, refine skipped below full, shapes limited to the
   level), summary read-back and JS contract tests.
7. docs/user-guide.md, docs/architecture.md,
   docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-13-pattern-detection-design.md - describe the
   detail levels and the measured rationale.

